# PHASE 16 — FALSE-POSITIVE TEST SUITE

Create comprehensive automated tests for the following cases.

| Scenario | Expected behavior |
|---|---|
| One ISP cannot access a server | Do not mark expired |
| Another ISP can access the server | Active or ISP restricted |
| Private RFC1918 IP | Preserve and exempt from public dead-domain classification |
| One resolver returns NXDOMAIN | Suspected or unverified |
| Multiple resolvers disagree | Unknown or suspected |
| SERVFAIL | Temporary DNS failure |
| DNS timeout | Temporary DNS failure |
| HTTP 401 | Authentication required / not expired |
| HTTP 403 | Forbidden / not expired |
| HTTP 404 on one path | Endpoint unavailable / domain not expired |
| HTTP 410 | Investigate; do not automatically remove |
| HTTP 429 | Rate limited / not expired |
| HTTP 500 | Server error / not expired |
| TLS certificate error | TLS failure / not expired |
| FTP authentication failure | Authentication failure / not expired |
| Domain lookup unavailable | Unknown |
| `.bd` registration source unavailable | Unknown |
| Stale ISP probe data | Do not treat as current proof |
| No ISP probe data | Unverified |
| Confirmed domain deletion | Eligible for removal review |
| User restores archived entry | Original entry restored |

Tests must be deterministic and must not depend on real external servers.

